,"user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure if the UndoRedo icon is appropriate, but it gives the impression that it sets the current key value to the Reset animation's Value. As I said, the actual behavior is to transfer the value to the currently unseen Reset animation, which is not intuitive.\r\n\r\nAlthough no actual issues have been reported, the main problem is that the Options menu contains a similar “Apply RESET” option. Having two options with arrows indicating reversal is quite confusing.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"469\" height=\"282\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d377c62a-30bf-4806-b0be-4cf09d021053\" />\r\n\r\n\"Apply RESET\" takes effect immediately on the current state, so the back arrow is appropriate. However, since “Add RESET Value” does nothing to the current animation, it should not reuse icons that indicate something happening immediately elsewhere.\r\n","created_at":"2025-10-03T14:23:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-03T14:26:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/11048